            <div xml:id="d792">

                <pb facs="1080" n="1068" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg1068"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">895.01/10–445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-04">October 4,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received October 8—4:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. If the directive which will legally separate Japan and Korea could be
                    promulgated in the very near future (the Supreme Commander to have the
                    discretion, of course, as to the exact date of issuance), we feel that it would
                    be a most timely move and would be universally pleasing to the Korean people and
                    would have the effect of assuaging their disappointments. Therefore, it is our
                    suggestion that the directive in question (which was being considered at the
                    time when I left Washington) be completed and telegraphed as soon as possible to
                    GHQ.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
